e rebuilt on current trunk.\n\n**Why this run existed.** Revision 1 of the Change Request was accepted against trunk 48db30b. Trunk then moved to a351afd when the configuration Story landed, and it touched three paths this fix also changes: the README, the traceability ownership registry, and the digest pin in traceability.go. Under the workspace contract that demotes the acceptance to stale, so the candidate had to be rebuilt and republished as revision 2.\n\n**What I changed.**\n- Rebased the story branch onto local main with signing. The only conflict was the registry digest pin at `internal/traceability/traceability.go:42`, where both sides had repinned for their own new tests.\n- Resolved it by taking trunk's file, letting tracecheck fail closed on the trunk digest, and repinning to the merged-registry projection digest. The registry JSON and README merged cleanly and keep both the config rows and the nesting-depth rows.\n- Added one logbook entry recording that the digest pin is a guaranteed conflict line between any two in-flight Stories that register evidence tests.\n- The fix itself is byte-identical to revision 1: the 256-level bound in decodeValue with typed refusal, inherited by Canonicalize and both identity entries.\n\nNew signed head is 3e48785 with a351afd as its parent, working tree clean. The pre-rebase tip ef0c1a5 is preserved in the reflog and as a patch under `.temp/BUG-260902-lyhvkw/refresh/`.\n\n**Gates rerun on the merged tree, all with real exit codes.** gofmt, vet, build on darwin, linux, and windows, catalog check, tracecheck full and per section, verbose tests, coverage, race on canonicaljson, and the three fuzz seeds all exited 0. A final test, vet, build, and tracecheck pass ran on the exact amended head and exited 0.\n\n| Package | Trunk a351afd | Head 3e48785 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| internal/canonicaljson | 87.1% | 87.2% |\n| every other package | unchanged | unchanged |\n\n**Mutants of the bound.** Widen to 512, widen to 257, narrow to 128, narrow to 255, and delete the gate all exit 1. The delete-gate mutant reproduces the original fatal stack overflow through the 2 MB regression test.\n\nEvidence is attached on the board as the four resources suffixed `-refresh-a351afd`, and board notes record the refresh. Revision 2 now needs a reviewer, and the orchestrator owns integration into trunk.","ttft_ms":2919,"type":"result","duration_ms":476528,"uuid":"5c23cca7-154f-4b7a-937d-2726b342bc16","ttft_stream_ms":2553,"time_to_request_ms":19,"queued_turn_count":0}
